"pyproject.toml\") |  [ Fix: change hiredis version to >= 3.0.0 (#216) ](/root/sotopia/-/commit/7f5be99bc1f8295a53428502843f24b41135b4f9 \"Fix: change hiredis version to >= 3.0.0 \\\\(#216\\\\)\\n\\n* change to >=\\r\\n\\r\\n* update poetry lock\\r\\n\\r\\n* typo\") |  1 year ago   \\n  \\n[ **README.md** ](/root/sotopia/-/blob/main/README.md?ref_type=heads)\\n\\n[ ](/root/sotopia/-/raw/main/figs/title.png)\\n\\n#  Sotopia: an Open-ended Social Learning Environment \\n\\n[ ](https://pypi.python.org/pypi/sotopia) [ ](https://github.com/sotopia/sotopia) [ ](https://github.com/sotopia-lab/sotopia/actions?query=branch%3Amain) [ ](https://codecov.io/github/sotopia-lab/sotopia) [ ](https://colab.research.google.com/drive/14hJOfzpA37PRUzdlFgiqVzUGIhhngqnz?usp=sharing)\\n\\n[ ](https://www.sotopia.world/projects/sotopia) [ ](https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.11667) [ ](https://huggingface.co/datasets/cmu-lti/sotopia) [ ](https://huggingface.co/spaces/cmu-lti/sotopia-space/)\\n\\n##  <::after> News \\n\\n  * <::marker>[05/2024] Sotopia was presented at ICLR 2024 as a spotlight \u2b50! \\n\\n\\n\\n##  <::after> Introduction \\n\\nSotopia is an open-ended social learning environment that allows agents to interact with each other and the environment. The environment is designed to be a platform for evaluating and faciliating social intelligence in language agents. The environment is designed to be open-ended, meaning that the environment can be easily extended to include new environments and new agents. The environment is also designed to be scalable, meaning that the environment can be easily scaled to include a large number of agents and environments. \\n    \\n    \\n    @inproceedings{zhou2024sotopia,\\n      title = {SOTOPIA: Interactive Evaluation for Social Intelligence in Language Agents},\\n      author = {Zhou*, Xuhui and Zhu*, Hao and Mathur, Leena and Zhang, Ruohong and Qi, Zhengyang and Yu, Haofei and Morency, Louis-Philippe and Bisk, Yonatan and Fried, Daniel and Neubig, Graham and Sap, Maarten},\\n      journal = {ICLR},\\n      year = {2024},\\n      url = {https://openreview.net/forum?id=mM7VurbA4r},\\n    }\\n\\n##  <::after> Help \\n\\nSee [ documentation ](https://docs.sotopia.world) for more details. \\n\\n##  <::after> Get started \\n\\n###  <::after> Install locally \\n\\nWe recommend using a virtual environment, e.g. with anaconda3: ` conda create -n sotopia python=3.11; conda activate sotopia; curl -sSL https://install.python-poetry.org | python3 ` . \\n\\nThen: ` python -m pip install sotopia; sotopia install `\\n\\nThis will setup the necessary environment variables and download the necessary data. \\n\\n> [!TIP] Having trouble installing? Or don\\'t want to install redis for now? We are working on a public redis server for you to use. Stay tuned! \\n\\nOpenAI key is required to run the code. Please set the environment variable ` OPENAI_API_KEY ` to your key. The recommend way is to add the key to the conda environment: \\n    \\n    \\n    conda env config vars set OPENAI_API_KEY=your_key\\n\\n##  <::after> Easy Sample Server \\n\\nYou can view an episode demo with default parameters with the following: \\n    \\n    \\n    import asyncio\\n    from sotopia.samplers import UniformSampler\\n    from sotopia.server import run_async_server\\n    \\n    asyncio.run(\\n        run_async_server(\\n            model_dict={\\n                \"env\": \"gpt-4\",\\n                \"agent1\": \"gpt-4o-mini\",\\n                \"agent2\": \"gpt-4o-mini\",\\n            },\\n            sampler=UniformSampler(),\\n        )\\n    )\\n\\nor run \\n    \\n    \\n    python examples/minimalist_demo.py\\n', url='http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/sotopia', trigger_by_action='browse_interactive', error=False, observation='browse', goal_image_urls=[], open_pages_urls=['http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/sotopia'], active_page_index=0, last_browser_action=\"goto('http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/sotopia')\\nnoop(1200)\\nscroll(0, 800)\\nnoop(500)\", last_browser_action_error='', focused_element_bid='85'), BrowseInteractiveAction(browser_actions=\"goto('http://the-agent-company.com:8929/admin/projects')\\nnoop(1200)\", thought='', browsergym_send_msg_to_user='', action='browse_interactive', security_risk=None), BrowserOutputObservation(content=\"Skip to main content \\n\\n##  Primary navigation \\n\\n[ Homepage  ](/)\\n\\nCreate new... \\n\\n  *     * [ New project/repository  ](/projects/new)\\n    * [ New group  ](/groups/new)\\n    * [ New snippet  ](/-/snippets/new)\\n\\n\\n\\nAdministrator user\u2019s menu \\n\\n  *     * [ Administrator  @root  ](/root)\\n  *     * Set status \\n    * [ Edit profile  ](/-/user_settings/profile)\\n    * [ Preferences  ](/-/profile/preferences)\\n  *     * [ Sign out  ](/users/sign_out)\\n\\n\\n\\n[ 84  ](/dashboard/issues?assignee_username=root)\\n\\n99+ \\n\\n  * Merge requests \\n\\n    * [ Assigned  7  ](/dashboard/merge_requests?assignee_username=root)\\n    * [ Review requests  157  ](/dashboard/merge_requests?reviewer_username=root)\\n\\n\\n\\n[ ](/dashboard/todos)\\n\\nSearch or go to\u2026 \\n\\nAdmin area \\n\\n  * Overview \\n\\n    * [ Dashboard  ](/admin)\\n    * [ Projects  ](/admin/projects)\\n    * [ Users  ](/admin/users)\\n    * [ Groups  ](/admin/groups)\\n    * [ Topics  ](/admin/topics)\\n    * [ Gitaly servers  ](/admin/gitaly_servers)\\n\\n  * CI/CD \\n\\n    * [ Runners  ](/admin/runners)\\n    * [ Jobs  ](/admin/jobs)\\n\\n  * Analytics \\n\\n    * [ DevOps Reports  ](/admin/dev_ops_reports)\\n    * [ Usage trends  ](/admin/usage_trends)\\n\\n  * Monitoring \\n\\n    * [ System information  ](/admin/system_info)\\n    * [ Background migrations  ](/admin/background_migrations)\\n    * [ Background jobs  ](/admin/background_jobs)\\n    * [ Health check  ](/admin/health_check)\\n\\n  * [ Messages  ](/admin/broadcast_messages)\\n  * [ System hooks  ](/admin/hooks)\\n  * [ Applications  ](/admin/applications)\\n  * [ Abuse rep